urname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Meindl</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamrick</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lovejoy</surname><given-names>CO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Patterns of correlation and covariation of anthropoid distal forelimb segments correspond to Hoxd expression territories.</article-title><source>J Exp Zoolog B Mol Dev Evol</source><year>2007</year><comment>doi:10.1002/jez.b.21207.</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vargas</surname><given-names>AO</given-names></name><name><surname>Fallon</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The digits of the wing of birds are 1, 2, and 3. A review.</article-title><source>J Exp Zoolog B Mol Dev Evol</source><year>2005</year><volume>304</volume><fpage>206</fpage><lpage>219</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15880771</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/jez.b.21051</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dahn</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Fallon</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interdigital regulation of digit identity and homeotic transformation by modulated BMP signaling.</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2000</year><volume>289</volume><fpage>438</fpage><lpage>441</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10903202</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.289.5478.438</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Dahn</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Shubin</surname><given-names>NH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An autopodial-like pattern of Hox expression in fins of a basal actinopterygian fish.</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2007</year><volume>447</volume><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>476</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17522683</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nature05838</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johanson</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Joss</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Boisvert</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ericsson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sutija</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahlberg</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fish fingers: digit homology in sarcopterygian fish fins.</article-title><source>J Exp Zoolog B Mol Dev Evol</source><year>2007</year><volume>308</volume><fpage>757</fpage><lpage>768</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17849442</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/jez.b.21197</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Freitas</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohn</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biphasic Hoxd gene expression in shark paired fins reveals an ancient origin of distal limb domain.</article-title><source>PLoS ONE</source><year>2007</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>e754</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17710153</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000754</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Prud'homme</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Gompel</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Rokas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kassner</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>TM</given-names></name><name><surname>Yeh</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>True</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Carroll</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Repeated morphological evolution through <italic>cis</italic>-regulatory changes in a pleiotropic gene.</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2006</year><volume>440</volume><fpage>1050</fpage><lpage>1053</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16625197</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nature04597</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>